430	42,436,380,940 - 318,436,380,560 - 350,780,380,940	430. Calyx and corolla of Thrift; separated.	The Thrift flower taken apart: above, the corolla of five narrow petals joined only at the base, a stamen before each; below, the dry, scaly funnel-shaped calyx.
431	318,436,516,940 - 318,480,332,560 - 318,580,382,640	431. Pistil of the same, with its 5 styles: also the lower part of an ovary more magnified, cut across.	Above, the Thrift pistil, a single small ovary with five slender styles curling out from its top; below, the base of an ovary cut across, more magnified.
